%N A399867 Number of equivalence classes of 0-1 matrices with n distinct rows and distinct nonzero columns, under row and column permutations.
%C A399867 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic T0 hypergraphs on n vertices without the empty edge. A hypergraph is T0 if for every pair of distinct vertices x and y there is an edge containing exactly one of x and y.
%C A399867 The number of equivalence classes when the zero column is also allowed is 2*a(n).
%C A399867 Next term is too large to include.
%H A399867 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399867/b399867.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..11</a>
%e A399867 For n=3, using 12 to denote the edge {1,2}, etc., the 32 nonisomorphic T0 hypergraphs without the empty edge can be represented by {1,2}, {1,12}, {12,13}, {1,2,3}, {1,2,12}, {1,2,13}, {1,2,123}, {1,12,13}, {1,12,23}, {1,12,123}, {12,13,23}, {12,13,123}, {1,2,3,12}, {1,2,3,123}, {1,2,12,13}, {1,2,12,123}, {1,2,13,23}, {1,2,13,123}, {1,12,13,23}, {1,12,13,123}, {1,12,23,123}, {12,13,23,123}, {1,2,3,12,13}, {1,2,3,12,123}, {1,2,12,13,23}, {1,2,12,13,123}, {1,2,13,23,123}, {1,12,13,23,123}, {1,2,3,12,13,23}, {1,2,3,12,13,123}, {1,2,12,13,23,123}, {1,2,3,12,13,23,123}.
%Y A399867 Cf. A059084-A059089 (labeled T0 hypergraphs), A094000 (0-1 matrices with distinct rows and columns), A049311 (0-1 matrices up to row and column permutations).
